{"text": "BRIANNA WILLIS\n\nhttps://www.briannawillistv.com/\n\n(323) 423-6315 | briannawillistv @ gmail.com\n\nvy\n\nin @briannawillistv\n\nEducation\n\nPepperdine University\nBachelor of Arts, Journalism\nMalibu, CA,\nAugust 2017 - May 2021\n\nBuenos Aires, Argentina\nSeptember 2018 - December 2018\n\nSkills\n\ne Inception, iNEWS, Dalet\nGalaxy, LiveU, Reporting,\nCanon XF 205, Social Media\nReporting (Twitter, Facebook,\nInstagram)\ne Adobe Premiere and Adobe\nPhotoshop\ne Wordpress, Camayak CMS,\nBrightspot CMS, HTML,\nWord, PowerPoint, Excel,\nOutlook, Google Docs\ne Leadership, Public Speaking,\nConflict Resolution\n\nAwards\n\ne ACP Pacemaker - Climate\nChange Reporting (3rd place)\ne TV32 Best Associate\nProducer (2020)\ne Best All-Around Contributor,\nCurrents Magazine (2020)\ne TV32 Best Associate Field\nReporter (2019)\ne TV32 Rookie of the Year\n(2018)\n\nProfessional Experience\n\nNewsWaves32, Pepperdine University\nAugust 2017 - Present Reporter/Anchor/EP\ne Executive produced Pepperdine's first fully remote weekly news show\n\u00a2 Multi-media journalist reporting, filming, editing and fronting packages live\nwith local content from Malibu & Calabasas communities\ne Executive produced, anchored, and reported for NewsWaves Connection's\nspecial edition shows\n\nPepperdine Graphic Media, Pepperdine University\nJanuary 2020 - Present Digital Editor, Social Media Team\n\u00a2 Oversee all social media platforms, report breaking news to all social\nplatforms and edit social team copy for every story on social\n\u00a2 Edit as the last line of defense and publish all content to the Graphic website\n\nFox News Media, Chicago/Dallas Bureau (Remote)\nFebruary 2021 - Present College Associate News Intern\ne Assist network reporters and producers on stories by writing, researching\nand reporting\n\u00a2 Cover press conferences and keep up to date with the news in the 18 states\nthe Chicago and Dallas Bureau's cover (Midwest and Southwest states)\n\nCrown Media Family Networks, Studio City, CA\nJune 2017 - February 2021 Production Assistant/Intern\ne Produce online content for the Hallmark Channel, Hallmark Movies &\nMysteries websites and Hallmark Channel Checklist App\ne Create microsites for movies/series with photo assets, games, quizzes,\nhighlight videos, cast bios and more\ne Attend interdepartmental meetings to pitch ideas for sales campaigns and\nassess request for proposals from potential partners\n\nSpectrum News! SoCal, El Segundo, CA\nJanuary 2020 - April 2020\ne Learn to stack and write for a hyperlocal newscast\ne Understand what is newsworthy, turn national stories into local stories\n\u00a2 Shadow journalists while out on stories and learn to create similar content\n\nGeneral News Intern",
